# Base URL of the Harmonia backend API that the frontend calls (Vite).
#
# You almost certainly do not need this. Leave it unset and the frontend calls
# the API on the same origin the page was served from, which is correct for the
# launchers, for Docker, and for `npm run dev` (the dev server proxies /api to
# the backend on port 8000, see vite.config.js).
#
# Set it only when the backend genuinely lives somewhere else, for example a
# frontend served from one host and an API on another:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8000
#
# Setting it to an absolute host that is not where the page came from will make
# every call cross-origin, and the backend allowlist (CORS_ORIGINS) has to be
# widened to match or the browser will discard responses the server processed.
